# Sega System 16B audio section -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Couriersud's netlist of the audio section of the System 16B CPU board, used for every
# System 16B game in MAME. The two YM3012 channels arrive as ports (CH1, CH2: MAME feeds
# the YM2151's output in directly and replaces the YM3012's sample-and-hold with the
# two RCOM resistors, as its file explains), and the uPD7759's speech as a current sink
# (SPEECH). The two op-amps are D20 (TL084) and XC20 (LM324): MAME's X keeps the IC at
# C20 apart from the capacitor C20, and both are written by position here, UD20 and UC20.
# VR1 is a resistor in MAME that is 'actually a potentiometer'.
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/sega/nl_segas16b.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(segas16b_audio). Licence CC0-1.0 by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Couriersud (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/sega/nl_segas16b.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# line 168: NET_C(GND, XC20.13, XC20.12, D20.13, D20.12, D20.2, D20.3) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Not connected" block
# line 169: NET_C(GND, XC20.14, D20.14, D20.1) -> nc -- tied to GND in MAME's "Not connected" block
# line 145: AMP_IN is not a part -- a 100K MAME assumes for the M51516L amplifier's input
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): CS(SPEECH)
#
# MAME's file marks its own doubts, and they are kept as it has them. It puts the mixer
# stage on XC20 pins 9, 8 and 10 where, its comments say, the schematic reads 9, 7 and 8 --
# 7 is already the speech filter's output, so MAME moved the stage onto the third section
# and asks 'other AMP?' of each. C19 and C22 'need verification', and the op-amps' supply
# is assumed: 'no information on schematics, assume 12V'. The site holds no System 16B
# schematic to settle any of it.
#
# Not compared with the sheet. MAME's designators, values and pin numbers are taken as
# MAME has them; the checker shows the netlist is internally consistent (every pin exists,
# no two outputs fight, nothing floats), which is not the same as matching the board.

# part UC20 LM324  (MAME: XC20)
# part UD20 TL084

value R3 10K
value R4 10K
value R5 10K
value R6 10K
value R7 47K
value R9 47K
value R10 47K
value R11 1K
value R12 1.3K
value R13 6.2K
value R14 5.6K
value R15 12K
value R16 6.8K
value RCOM1 390
value RCOM2 390
value VR1 2K  # MAME's comment: 'FIXME: Actually a potentiometer'
value C12 10uF
value C19 47uF  # MAME's comment: 'FIXME: Needs verification'
value C20 1000pF
value C21 2.2uF
value C22 2.2uF  # MAME's comment: 'Needs verification'
value C23 0.022uF
value C24 0.01uF
value C25 0.0022uF
value C26 0.022uF
value C28 1500pF
value C29 1500pF
value C62 2.2uF
value C63 2.2uF

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supplies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net GND: C19.2 C24.2 C25.2 C28.2 C29.2 UD20.11 R16.2 R5.2 VR1.2 UC20.11
net +12V: UD20.4 UC20.4
net +5V: R11.1 R4.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YM2151/YM3012 inputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port CH1: RCOM1.1  # in MAME: ANALOG_INPUT(CH1)
wire C29.1 UD20.5 RCOM1.2
wire C22.1 UD20.6 UD20.7
port CH2: RCOM2.1  # in MAME: ANALOG_INPUT(CH2)
wire C28.1 UD20.10 RCOM2.2
wire C21.1 UD20.8 UD20.9

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Speech inputs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port SPEECH: R11.2 R14.1  # in MAME: CS(SPEECH)
wire C26.1 R14.2 R15.1 R16.1
wire C25.1 R15.2 UC20.5
wire C26.2 R12.1 UC20.6 UC20.7
wire C23.1 R12.2 R13.1
wire C24.1 R13.2 UC20.3
wire C23.2 C62.1 UC20.1 UC20.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mixing and pre amplifier
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire C62.2 R6.1
wire C22.2 R9.1
wire C21.2 R10.1
wire C20.1 R10.2 R6.2 R7.1 R9.2 UC20.9
wire C20.2 C63.1 R7.2 UC20.8
wire C19.1 R4.2 R5.1 UC20.10
wire C63.2 R3.1
wire C12.1 R3.2 VR1.1
port OUT: C12.2  # to the power amplifier (an M51516L, MAME's file says), which MAME does not simulate

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins with nothing attached
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
nc UC20.13 UC20.12 UD20.13 UD20.12 UD20.2 UD20.3  # line 168: tied to GND in MAME's "Not connected" block
nc UC20.14 UD20.14 UD20.1  # line 169: tied to GND in MAME's "Not connected" block
